  "col_left L3, L5, L31: «Mūsà» (five times) is printed with a grave accent on the final a.",
  "col_left L6: «(= Omar)» is printed with a long equals sign; «Omar» in the parenthesis has no sign of ‘ayn, as printed.",
  "col_left L9: the marks over the i of «Sa‘īd», «as-Sūsī» and both i of «al-Marghītī» are bars (1.8–2.8 by 1.0–1.1 points).",
  "col_left L12: «Sibṭ» has the dot under the t; «al-Māridīnī» has a dot over the first i (1.3 by 1.4 points) and bars over the second and the last (2.4–2.5 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_left L13, L14: «IX» is printed in full capitals (7.6 points tall), «{sc:xv}» in small capitals; transcribed as printed.",
  "col_left L14, L15: «*I manoscritti*» and «*arabi. . . . . della Bibl. Naz. di Torino*» are printed in italics; after «arabi» a point and four more points stand 4.2–5.3 points apart.",
  "col_left L18: «aṭ-Ṭayyib» has the dots under the t and the T; the mark over the last i of «al-‘Alamī» is a short bar (1.7 by 0.8 points).",
  "col_left L19: «Muḥyī» has the ḥ sort and a bar over the i (2.3 by 1.1 points); «al-Maghrabī» a bar (2.5 by 1.1 points); «Yaḥyà» the ḥ sort and a grave accent on the a.",
  "col_left L26, L30: «*adh-dhirā‘ayn*» and «al-‘arūs» have the sign of ‘ayn.",
  "col_left L30: «Murtaḍà» has the dot under the d and a grave accent on the a; «az-Zabīdī» has bars over both i (2.3 by 1.0 and 1.9 by 1.0 points); «Tāǵ» is printed with ǵ, Nallino's sign for jīm.",
  "col_left L33: «*al-mutaqaddim li ’l-qaṭāf*» is printed in italics, with the apostrophe of elision and the dot under the t; «ε» is Greek.",
  "col_left L34: «al-Mu‘taṣim» has the sign of ‘ayn and the dot under the s; its hyphen is printed short (2.0 by 1.1 points).",
  "col_left L36: the Syriac «ܡܘܙܓܐ» (mūzāgā) is printed in Serto without vowel points, read at 4,800 dpi: mim, waw, zain, gamal with its descending tail, and a final alaph.",
  "col_left L36, L37: a blank line separates the names in M from those in N. A speck (1.6 by 2.0 points) in the blank line, 10–12 points above the baseline of L37, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L37: «*an-na‘ā’im*» has the sign of ‘ayn, a bar over the second a and the sign ’; the 6 of «296» is printed broken.",
  "col_left L39: «Bukhtanaṣṣar» has the dots under both s.",
  "col_left L41: «an-Nabtītī» has bars over both i (2.3 by 1.0–1.1 points); «‘Alī» has the sign of ‘ayn and a bar. A hairline (2.5 by 0.6 points) to the right of the last bar of «an-Nabtītī», 8.7–9.9 points above the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L42: «*nāḍikā*» has the dot under the d and bars over both a.",
  "col_left L43: «an-Nadīm» has a bar over the i (2.3 by 1.0 points); its N is printed broken, its left stem in pieces.",
  "col_left L45: the 3 of «n. 3», the 0 of «320» and the first 1 of «211» are printed broken; read as the figures.",
  "col_right L6: «an-Nasawī» has a bar over the i (2.5 by 1.0 points). The comma after it is printed without its tail: a small teardrop (1.4 by 1.9 points, its foot 0.4 point below the baseline), narrower than the round points of the page (1.7–2.0 points), like a point at low resolution; read at 8,000 dpi as the head of a comma, which separates a name from the name that follows in the index (as «al-Khayyāṭ, Abū ‘Alī Yaḥyà», p. 392). The second a of «Aḥmad» is printed blotted.",
  "col_right L7, L8: «an-Nāṣir» and «Naṣīr» have the dot under the s; «‘Alnās» begins with the sign of ‘ayn; the N of «an-Nāṣir» is printed broken.",
  "col_right L8: «aṭ-Ṭūsī» has the dots under the t and the T and a bar over the last i (2.2 by 1.1 points).",
  "col_right L12, L14: «*aṭ-ṭā’ir*» has the dots under both t and the sign ’; «*al-wāqi‘*» ends with the sign of ‘ayn; «α» is Greek in both lines.",
  "col_right L16: the v of «nativitates» is printed broken, the top of its left arm apart from the letter; read v. «*mawālīd*» has bars over the a and the i.",
  "col_right L22: «his» after «*148*» is printed with an h, read at 4,800 dpi: its counter is open at the foot and both stems end in a foot serif, unlike the closed bowl of the b in the word bis of L8 and L25. It stands for bis (p. 148 twice); transcribed as printed.",
  "col_right L17, L21, L22: several t's are printed without the left part of their crossbar, like l («nativitatum», «errantium», «tabulae»); read t.",
  "col_right L27: the h of «Vh.» is printed broken, like lı.",
  "col_right L28: «*naw’*» and «*anwā’*» end with the sign of hamza.",
  "col_right L30: «*nawrōz*» has a bar over the o; «67» is upright.",
  "col_right L31: «an-Nayrīzī» has bars over both i (2.4 by 1.1 and 2.3 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_right L33: a speck (1.8 by 1.3 points) to the right of the line, 2.5–3.8 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L34: «*nayzĕkā*» has a breve over the e and a bar over the last a. The Syriac «ܢܝܙܟܐ» (nayzkā) is printed in Serto without vowel points, read at 4,800 dpi: nun, yod, zain, kaph and a final alaph.",
  "col_right L41: the h of «Nicephorus» is printed with its two foot serifs joined, so that its counter is closed at the foot like b; read h.",
